WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.096
The saved Week 16 index lists eleven reading rows. The assigned focus ranges from learner-specific remediation to procedure review, provincial examination material, case reasoning, medication review and measurement flashcards.
已保存的第16周索引列出十一项阅读，主题包括针对个人弱项的补强、操作指南复习、省级考试资料、案例推理、药物复习和测量闪卡。

00:00:15.096 --> 00:00:30.048
Nancy Caroline’s Canadian eighth edition is the learner-confirmed principal examination text. The selected assessment chapters below are a separate bridge; they are not a twelfth school row and do not replace any of the eleven assignments.
Nancy Caroline加拿大第八版是学习者确认的主考试教材。下文选取的评估章节是额外衔接内容，不是学校第十二项阅读，也不能替代十一项指定阅读。

00:00:30.048 --> 00:00:51.384
The reading panel now contains the reviewed school-folder bodies rather than short candidate placeholders. Keep three distinctions visible: a named chapter can be explained even when a school page number conflicts; a checklist index is not every listed procedure body; and a current clinical comparison is not proof of the school edition.
阅读面板现已接入审阅过的学校文件夹正文，不再只有简短候选占位。要区分三点：学校页码冲突时仍可讲解具名章节；核查表目录不等于其中每项完整操作；现行临床对照不证明学校使用该版本。

00:00:51.384 --> 00:01:19.416
The cardiovascular copy has seventy-nine physical pages, while the school locator reaches page three hundred nineteen. The complete seven named chapters are explained, but literal page equivalence is unresolved. The procedure reader now adds primary Pinel teaching and distinguishes the actual PR30 resources from the mislabeled attachment. Source identity differences remain visible rather than becoming invented instructions.
心血管副本共七十九个物理页，学校定位却到三百一十九页。七个具名章已完整讲解，但字面页码对应仍未解决。规程阅读现加入原始Pinel教学，并区分真实PR30资源和错误标签附件。保留来源身份差异，不能将其变成编造指令。

00:01:19.416 --> 00:01:34.200
For a case-focused chapter, build a timeline and separate reported facts, direct observations, unknowns and assumptions. For a skills checklist, identify the safety gate, expected result and reassessment point.
阅读案例章节时，先建立时间线，并区分转述事实、直接观察、未知信息和假设。阅读技能核查表时，应找出安全关口、预期结果和复评节点。

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:51.480
Keep source identity beside each note. A candidate nursing or pharmacology textbook can explain a general concept, but current BC Emergency Health Services direction, BC legislation, provider scope and instructor guidance control operational practice.
每条笔记旁都要标明来源。候选护理或药理教材可以解释一般概念，但实际操作以BCEHS现行指示、BC法规、执业权限和教师指导为准。

00:01:51.480 --> 00:02:11.088
Start with the assignment directory in Reading mode. The cardiovascular guide has all seven chapter routes, the pharmacology guide has twenty-five chapters in six units, and the procedure guide has code-specific rounds. These are organized components of weekly teaching, not hundreds of unrelated lessons.
先在阅读模式使用指定阅读目录。心血管指南有七章路径，药理指南按六单元排列二十五章，操作指南有逐编号轮次。这些是每周教学的有序组成，不是几百个互不相关的课程。

00:02:11.088 --> 00:02:29.088
Read both the source notice and the explanation. When the school names an individual gap, select the matching route from an actual observed difficulty. Do not manufacture a personal deficiency or mark a missing school appendix complete because a related nursing index is available.
同时阅读来源说明和讲解。学校要求个人弱项时，应根据实际观察到的困难选择路径。不要虚构个人缺陷，也不要因取得相关护理目录就把缺失的学校附录标为完成。

00:02:29.088 --> 00:02:52.680
For the school bradycardia case, connect electrical rate to mechanical output. Cardiac output depends on both rate and stroke volume, and tissue perfusion also depends on pressure and vascular conditions. A low displayed rate alone does not tell you whether output is adequate. Compare consciousness, skin, symptoms, blood pressure and the measured trend.
针对学校心动过缓案例，将电活动频率连到机械输出。心输出量取决于心率和每搏量，组织灌注也受压力及血管状态影响。单凭屏幕低心率不能判断输出是否足够。要比较意识、皮肤、症状、血压和实测趋势。

00:02:52.680 --> 00:03:15.912
If the learner gap is respiratory, distinguish movement of air, gas exchange and oxygen delivery. If it is neurological, connect an observed change to brain function without assigning a lesion from one sign. The A&P routes support targeted explanation; they do not impose an invented fixed reading range on the school’s individualized assignment.
如果弱项是呼吸，要区分空气移动、气体交换和氧输送；如果是神经，要把观察变化联系到脑功能，而不是凭单一体征定位病灶。A&P路径支持针对性解释，不为学校个体化作业编造固定阅读页。

00:03:15.912 --> 00:03:41.040
Read the seven chapters as one circulation: electrical activation drives contraction; filling and resistance affect flow; valve or congenital abnormalities alter pressure or direction; and coronary supply must meet demand. Heart failure can occur with preserved ejection fraction, so a preserved fraction does not prove normal filling pressures or absence of congestion.
把七章读成同一循环：电激动驱动收缩，充盈及阻力影响流量，瓣膜或先天异常改变压力或方向，冠脉供血必须满足需求。射血分数保留也可出现心衰，因此分数保留不能证明充盈压正常或没有淤血。

00:03:41.040 --> 00:04:06.408
In a breathless patient, contrast pump failure with an arrhythmia, an ischaemic process and a non-cardiac cause instead of forcing every cue into one diagnosis. New chest symptoms, a changing ECG or a concerning perfusion trend require the authorized assessment and escalation pathway. A summary table is not a rule that excludes disease when one familiar sign is absent.
气短患者要比较泵衰、心律失常、缺血及非心源原因，不能把所有线索硬塞进一个诊断。新胸部症状、心电图变化或令人担忧的灌注趋势，应按获准评估与升级路径处理。不能因缺少某个熟悉体征就用总结表排除疾病。

00:04:06.408 --> 00:04:27.480
Start the six-unit review with the difference between what the body does to a medicine and what a medicine does to the body. Poor intake, renal or hepatic impairment, timing and formulation can change exposure. A medicine list without the last actual dose or a recent change may conceal the most important part of the history.
六单元复习先区分身体怎样处理药物，以及药物怎样作用于身体。摄入差、肾肝功能受损、时间与剂型都会改变暴露。只有药单、没有最近实际服药时间或近期变更，可能遗漏最重要病史。

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:53.376
Use the early chapters for safe administration, legal and ethical reasoning, calculations, teaching, supplements and complementary products. An OTC label or natural origin does not remove interaction or toxicity risk. Dimensional analysis checks units, but the result still needs the correct patient, authorized order, concentration, route and a plausibility check.
前面章节用于安全给药、法律伦理推理、计算、教育及补充和辅助产品。非处方标签或天然来源不会消除相互作用与中毒风险。量纲分析检查单位，但结果仍需正确患者、获准医嘱、浓度、途径和合理性检查。

00:04:53.376 --> 00:05:15.912
The immunity, anti-infective and cancer chapters connect treatment targets with host risk. Distinguish immune suppression from immune stimulation and an allergic reaction from an unrelated adverse effect. An antibiotic does not treat every cause of fever, and changing symptoms can reflect a complication rather than failure to use a stronger drug.
免疫、抗感染与肿瘤章节将治疗靶点连到宿主风险。区分免疫抑制和刺激，也区分过敏与其他不良反应。抗生素不能治疗所有发热原因；症状变化可能是并发问题，而不只是没有使用更强药。

00:05:15.912 --> 00:05:41.664
In a recently treated cancer patient who becomes unwell, obtain the treatment and symptom timeline and assess immediate threats without assuming the problem is anxiety or an expected side effect. Report fever, deterioration and relevant treatment information through the actual pathway. This review explains risk recognition, not an independent antimicrobial or oncology prescription.
近期接受肿瘤治疗者不适时，应取得治疗及症状时间线并评估即时威胁，不能先认定是焦虑或正常副作用。按实际路径报告发热、恶化及相关治疗资料。本复习解释风险识别，不提供独立抗感染或肿瘤处方。

00:05:41.664 --> 00:06:07.104
Use the neural foundation before memorizing drug names. Receptor location and action explain why one product can change pulse, pressure, secretions, alertness or breathing. The same symptom can arise from illness, a prescribed dose, accumulation, a missed treatment or another exposure, so reconstruct the timeline before deciding which mechanism best fits.
先学神经基础再记药名。受体位置与作用能解释同一产品为何改变脉搏、血压、分泌、清醒度或呼吸。同一症状可来自疾病、处方剂量、蓄积、漏药或另一暴露，因此先重建时间线，再判断最符合的机制。

00:06:07.104 --> 00:06:34.200
The neurological, psychiatric and substance-use routes preserve important distinctions: withdrawal can occur despite a positive alcohol level; ongoing opioid agonist treatment is not simply a short weaning course; and apparent improvement after a reversal medicine may not last as long as the original exposure. Continue the required monitoring and communication rather than treating one response as a final diagnosis.
神经、精神及物质使用路径保留重要区别：血液仍有酒精也可发生戒断；持续阿片激动剂治疗不是单纯短期减量；逆转药后看似改善可能短于原暴露作用。应持续规定监测与沟通，不把一次反应当最终诊断。

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:58.896
Link cardiovascular drug purpose to the patient’s findings. A medicine that lowers pressure or slows the node may have a useful chronic role yet be relevant to today’s poor perfusion. Diuretics can change volume and electrolytes; treatment effect and adverse effect must be assessed together. Never infer that all slow rhythms or all rapid rhythms share one medication response.
将心血管药物目的连到患者发现。降压或减慢结点的药可能有长期价值，也可能与今天灌注差有关。利尿药改变容量及电解质；应同时评估治疗作用和不良作用。不能推断所有慢心律或所有快心律有相同药物反应。

00:06:58.896 --> 00:07:27.336
Antiplatelets, anticoagulants and thrombolytics act at different parts of haemostasis and have different indications, monitoring and reversal limits. A normal INR does not exclude clinically relevant direct oral anticoagulant exposure. Lipid treatments primarily address longer-term risk; symptom absence does not prove treatment is unnecessary. Use chapter contrasts before recalling a product from its name ending.
抗血小板、抗凝与溶栓作用于止血的不同环节，其适应证、监测及逆转限制不同。INR正常不能排除有临床意义的直接口服抗凝药暴露。降脂治疗主要应对长期风险；没有症状不证明不需治疗。先掌握章内比较，不只凭药名后缀回忆产品。

00:07:27.336 --> 00:07:52.848
The named sixth unit includes all three respiratory chapters, even though the school’s literal page endpoint stops earlier. Distinguish upper-airway symptom products, lower-airway bronchodilators and anti-inflammatory controllers. A brief improvement in wheeze does not prove all risk is resolved. An acceptable saturation does not prove that the patient is ventilating adequately.
第六命名单元包括全部三章呼吸内容，虽然学校字面页码较早结束。要区分上呼吸道缓症状产品、下呼吸道扩张剂与抗炎控制药。喘鸣短暂改善不证明所有风险解除。血氧饱和度看似合适，也不能证明患者通气足够。

00:07:52.848 --> 00:08:17.232
Check the actual formulation and delivery device before reasoning about benefit or harm. Children are not small adults for cough-and-cold products; combination ingredients and sedating effects matter. If a patient is deteriorating, reassess airway, breathing, mental status and authorized escalation needs instead of stacking OTC products or treating the monitor number alone.
判断获益和风险前要核对实际剂型与输送装置。儿童使用咳嗽感冒产品不能当小成人；复方成分及镇静作用都重要。患者恶化时，应复评气道、呼吸、意识和获准升级需要，而不是叠加非处方药或只处理监护数字。

00:08:17.232 --> 00:08:38.688
The code-specific reading rounds explain the available procedure bodies and identify advanced-provider material. For the two-hundred-twenty-kilogram movement case, capacity, patient condition, route and the whole equipment system must be assessed before movement. A patient’s ability to stand or an isolated device label cannot replace that plan.
逐编号阅读轮次解释可得操作正文并标明高级层级内容。针对二百二十公斤移动案例，移动前必须评估承载、患者状态、路线及整套设备系统。患者能站立或单一设备标签不能替代计划。

00:08:38.688 --> 00:09:05.496
For Pinel, use the actual manufacturer instructions together with the current service policies, not a title in an old contents page. For transfusion, explain the supplied checklist and pediatric syringe method within their actual roles. A volumetric label on a syringe manual does not change the device. Do not invent a missing method or turn a hospital example into new independent PCP authority.
Pinel应依据真实厂家说明及现行机构政策，而非旧目录标题。输血应按真实角色讲所提供核查表及儿科注射泵方法。注射泵手册上的体积泵标签不会改变器材。不能编造缺失方法，也不能将医院示例变成新的PCP独立权限。

00:09:05.496 --> 00:09:30.864
The CPSC guide groups the complete Appendix Two index and explains the assigned glucose-assessment pages. A checklist entry tells you that a procedure exists; it does not supply every instruction or make an unfamiliar ward skill appropriate for a PCP. Check indication, equipment, patient explanation, infection-control boundaries, response and the actual authorized procedure.
CPSC指南对完整附录二目录分组，并讲解指定血糖评估页。核查表条目说明某操作存在，不提供全部指令，也不会让陌生病房技能自动适用于PCP。要核对适应情境、设备、患者解释、感染控制边界、反应及实际获准流程。

00:09:30.864 --> 00:09:54.720
The CNS guide teaches the identified cardiac chapter and clinical-judgment content. Its missing Appendix Two pointer remains separate from the available CPSC index. Use cardiac assessment to connect history and physical findings, but do not let a checklist delay immediate support or convert an educational nursing assessment into a paramedic treatment order.
CNS指南讲解已识别心脏章节和临床判断内容；缺失的附录二定位仍与可得CPSC目录分开。用心脏评估联系病史及体征，但不要让清单延误即时支持，也不能将护理教学评估变成急救治疗医嘱。

00:09:54.720 --> 00:10:19.296
The Chapter Seven flashcards are technique retrieval, not just number memorization. Explain temperature method, pulse and respirations, pressure technique and saturation limitations. In the large-patient case, choose a cuff using the measured arm and manufacturer range; body weight does not determine cuff size. A poor fit can distort the pressure you use to judge perfusion.
第七章闪卡用于提取测量技术，不只是背数值。要解释测温方法、脉搏呼吸、血压技术及血氧限制。大体型案例应按实测臂围与厂商范围选袖带；体重不能决定袖带尺寸。贴合不佳会扭曲用于判断灌注的血压。

00:10:19.296 --> 00:10:41.616
When the measurement conflicts with appearance, check the method and signal, repeat appropriately and continue immediate care. Document why a reading is uncertain rather than silently discarding it or reporting false precision. The twelve source cards are reviewed in the guide; supervised practice still establishes hand position, fit and measurement quality.
测量与外观冲突时，应检查方法和信号，适当复测并继续即时照护。记录读数为何不确定，不能悄悄弃用或报告虚假精度。指南复习了原文十二张卡；手位、贴合及测量质量仍需监督实操确认。

00:10:41.616 --> 00:11:04.752
In the unfolding case, do not leak later information into an earlier decision. At each point state what is known now, its source, the important unknown and the priority it supports. A patient can improve in one domain while a functional, pain or safety problem remains. Reassessing only the number that first worried you can miss the next threat.
展开式案例不能把后来信息倒灌进早先决定。每个时点说明当前已知、来源、重要未知及其支持的优先级。患者某方面改善时，功能、疼痛或安全问题仍可存在。若只复查最初担心的数字，可能漏掉下一威胁。

00:11:04.752 --> 00:11:25.848
Use the FON clinical-judgment chain to explain why a new cue changes your plan. A changed plan is not proof that the first clinician was careless; it may reflect new information. Separate observation from interpretation, choose an action within current authority, then explain the actual response and the next decision.
用FON临床判断链解释新线索为何改变计划。计划改变不证明最初人员粗心，也可能因为新资料出现。区分观察与解释，选择现行权限内行动，再解释实际反应及下一决定。

00:11:25.848 --> 00:11:48.432
The MSN outcome-evaluation reading asks you to compare a planned result with evidence, not to count completed tasks. State the intended observable change, the actual finding, time and method. If breathing appears easier but consciousness falls, report both. You cannot call the overall goal met by selecting only the favourable result.
MSN结果评价要求将计划与证据比较，不是数完成了多少任务。说清预期可观察变化、实际发现、时间和方法。呼吸似乎轻松但意识下降时，两者都要报告。不能只挑有利结果就宣布总体目标达到。

00:11:48.432 --> 00:12:08.328
If a goal is not met, reassess the patient, original assumption, intervention delivery and measurement quality. Do not automatically repeat or intensify treatment. Communicate the expected-versus-actual response and unresolved concern so the next clinician can act on the same evidence.
目标未达到时，应复评患者、原假设、干预实施及测量质量，不能自动重复或强化治疗。交接预期与实际反应差异和未解决担忧，让下一位临床人员能依据同样证据行动。

00:12:08.328 --> 00:12:33.360
The mental-health case dissection separates what the person said, what you observed and what you infer. In an anxious or distressed patient, use calm neutral language, one question at a time and enough space to answer. Do not diagnose from a short fragment or allow a psychiatric history to explain away abnormal breathing, perfusion, glucose or consciousness.
精神健康案例剖析要区分本人说法、你的观察和你的推断。焦虑或痛苦患者应使用平静中性语言，一次一个问题并留足回答时间。不能凭片段诊断，也不能让精神病史掩盖呼吸、灌注、血糖或意识异常。

00:12:33.360 --> 00:12:58.776
Reassess safety and the response to communication as the case develops. Explain privacy without promising absolute secrecy when safety requires appropriate sharing. During debrief, identify the specific new fact that changed concern, the support you sought and what still needs follow-up. These are observable clinical behaviours rather than labels such as difficult or non-compliant.
随着案例发展，应复评安全及沟通反应。解释隐私，但不能在安全需要适当分享时承诺绝对保密。复盘时指出改变担忧的具体新事实、寻求的支持及仍需随访事项。这些是可观察临床行为，不是难搞或不配合等标签。

00:12:58.776 --> 00:13:24.144
The BC Provincial Examination Guidelines reader distinguishes the school’s saved version, the literal pages and the grading material reached by the named topic. It also identifies the later comparison rather than mixing editions. Provincial exam deficiencies and result-review procedures belong to that licensing system; they are not automatically AET Mock OSCE pass marks or critical-fail rules.
BCPEG阅读区分学校保存版本、字面页面及按具名主题找到的评分正文，并标明后续对照版，避免混版。省级考试缺陷类别及结果复核程序属于该执照系统，不自动成为AET模拟OSCE及格线或关键失败规则。

00:13:24.144 --> 00:13:48.000
Use feedback by recording the observed action, sequence, consequence and actual criterion, then choose one corrected behaviour for the next drill. The available school plan requires extensive documentation and formal handover. It does not supply a numerical station rubric, so neither an original practice answer nor a polished handover can certify a school pass.
利用反馈时应记录观察动作、顺序、后果和实际标准，再选下一次练习要修正的行为。可得学校计划要求详细记录与正式交接，但未提供数字站点量表，因此原创练习答案或流畅交接都不能认证学校及格。

00:13:48.000 --> 00:14:04.056
For each mock case, name one idea from the reading that changed your assessment, sequencing, measurement, documentation or handover. If no decision changed, explain what knowledge gap remains rather than forcing a textbook connection.
每个模拟案例都应指出阅读中的哪项知识改变了评估、操作顺序、测量、记录或交接。如果没有改变任何决策，就说明仍存在哪项知识缺口，不要硬套教材内容。

00:14:04.056 --> 00:14:16.488
A reading guide supports revision; it does not certify clinical competence. Only supervised school practice and the instructor’s actual criteria can establish performance in the assigned station.
阅读指南用于复习，不认证临床能力。只有学校监督下的练习和教师实际标准，才能评价指定站点的表现。

00:14:16.488 --> 00:14:42.000
Close the notes and walk through the school bradycardia and movement case from arrival to handover. State what you know and do not know. Explain which reading changes each decision: measurement for reliable pressure, cardiovascular and pharmacology reasoning for the clinical picture, procedures for safe movement, and case chapters for response and communication. Do not invent extra case observations.
合上笔记，从到场到交接走一遍学校心动过缓与移动案例。说明已知和未知，再解释每个决定由哪项阅读改变：测量支持可靠血压，心血管药理支持临床解释，操作支持安全移动，案例章节支持反应评价和沟通。不要增加虚构案例观察。

00:14:42.000 --> 00:15:05.232
When you cannot explain one step, reopen that exact chapter or round, then rehearse again using an actual observed gap. The aim is one coherent clinical performance, not recalling a pile of isolated facts. Reading completion, media playback, practical competence and official school assessment remain different kinds of evidence.
某一步解释不清时，重开对应章或轮次，再根据实际弱项排练。目标是连贯临床表现，不是回忆零散事实。阅读完成、媒体播放、实操能力及学校正式考核仍是不同证据。

00:15:05.232 --> 00:15:28.920
A frightened patient is not an equipment problem. Start with safety, communication and possible illness, and attempt reasonable de-escalation. If restraint becomes necessary, establish the applicable authority and seek appropriate clinical advice. Explain the plan and the conditions for ending it. A product demonstration cannot make that decision for you.
恐惧的患者不是一个器材问题。先顾安全、沟通及可能疾病，并尝试合理降级。若必须约束，确认适用权限并寻求适当临床建议。解释计划和解除条件，产品示范不能替你作决定。

00:15:28.920 --> 00:15:49.560
Use the least restrictive suitable method for the shortest necessary time. The reader distinguishes current service policies from the manufacturer instructions. It also identifies contradictions in those instructions. In supervised practice, name the actual model and approved configuration before describing how its parts connect.
以最小适当限制维持最短必要时间。阅读区分现行机构政策与厂家说明，也指出说明中的矛盾。监督练习时，应先说真实型号及获准配置，再描述部件连接。

00:15:49.560 --> 00:16:10.224
Before use, identify the compatible parts and demonstrate both locking and release. A click alone is not enough. During application, check fit and the actual attachment point, then assess breathing, skin and distal circulation. A later recheck never excuses an immediately unsafe fit.
使用前辨认匹配部件并演示锁闭和释放，单有咔嗒声不够。实施中核贴合及真实固定点，再评呼吸、皮肤和远端循环；之后复检不能成为暂时不安全贴合的借口。

00:16:10.224 --> 00:16:35.160
A waist belt, pelvic component and lateral attachments have different jobs. An extender changes length, not automatically load capacity. A manufacturer photograph with hands behind the body does not establish an approved transport position. Never place or transport a restrained person face down; follow the actual service policy and maintain patient access.
腰带、骨盆部件和侧向连接各有用途。延长带改长度，不自动改承重。厂家照片中的双手背后不证明转运体位获准。受约束者不得俯卧放置或转运；应按真实机构政策并保持可接近患者。

00:16:35.160 --> 00:16:57.912
In the original case, the patient becomes unusually quiet after restriction. Stop interpreting compliance as recovery. Reassess the airway, ventilation, perfusion and possible restraint-related harm, obtain help and coordinate safe adjustment or release with necessary support. Continue looking for the underlying medical cause.
原创案例中患者约束后异常安静，不能把配合当恢复。复评气道、通气、灌注及约束相关损害，求助并协调安全调整或释放和必要支持，同时继续寻找原发医学原因。

00:16:57.912 --> 00:17:21.096
Document the observed risk, alternatives, chosen method, response, monitoring, interventions and clinical communication. Explain what would permit discontinuation, reassess frequently and reduce restriction as soon as safe. Your rehearsal records observable decisions and omissions; it does not certify a skill or create an official school score.
记录观察风险、替代措施、所选方法、反应、监护、干预及临床沟通。说明解除条件，频繁复评，安全时尽早减少限制。排练记录可观察决定及遗漏，不签核技能，也不创造学校正式分数。
